      },
      {
        "content": "Given:\n- 10 breeding rabbits\n- First spring: 10 times as many kittens as breeding rabbits (10 * 10 = 100 kittens)\n- Half of the kittens got adopted (100 / 2 = 50 adopted, 50 remaining)\n- 5 kittens had to be returned (50 + 5 = 55 kittens)\n- Next spring: 60 kittens, 4 adopted (60 - 4 = 56 kittens)\n\nTotal rabbits after first spring: 10 breeding + 55 kittens = 65 rabbits\nTotal rabbits after second spring: 65 + 56 kittens = 121 rabbits\n\nThe exact-answer checker rejected the answer, so let's recheck the problem statement and calculations.\n\nRecheck:\n- First spring: 10 breeding rabbits, 100 kittens, 50 adopted, 5 returned, so 55 kittens remain.\n- Second spring: 60 kittens, 4 adopted, so 56 kittens remain.\n\nTotal rabbits: 10 breeding + 55 from first spring + 56 from second spring = 121 rabbits\n\nThe calculation was correct, but the exact-answer checker might have been looking for a specific format or a different approach. Let's ensure all steps are clear and restate the final answer.\n\nFINAL: 121",
